    "summary": "Pressed from the wall, the young colleague gives a deliberately vague testimony, and the manager takes it as proof.",
    "shots": "[Shot 1] Medium: 钱经理 (S3) finishes looking at the colleague and turns his eyes to her face, waiting; he lifts one hand off the desk and turns it over, palm up, a short beckoning motion that means go on. His lips stay closed.\n[Shot 2] At 00:02.000, closer on 小唐 (S4) standing on the open floor beside the desk: she draws her shoulders up, keeps her eyes on the floor tiles and lets them flick once toward 苏小满 (S1), then away; she speaks in a small thin nervous Mandarin, fast and slightly breathy: [Chinese] 钱经理。中午，我看见她往兜里塞东西。没看清。\n[Shot 3] At 00:08.400, reverse onto 苏小满 (S1) across the desk: her shoulders stay level, only her eyes travel to the girl by the door.\n[Shot 4] At 00:09.400, close on 钱经理 (S3) taking that in, the corner of his mouth pulling up, his lips closed for the rest of the shot.",
    "soundscape": "A thin nervous voice close to the lens, the fluorescent panels buzzing, a chair creaking somewhere behind the door, one dry swallow.",
    "music": "N/A",
    "crowd": false,
    "style_pack": "lean",
    "_lean_shots": "[Shot 1] Medium: 钱经理 (S3) finishes looking at the colleague and turns his eyes to her face, waiting; he lifts one hand off the desk and turns it over, palm up, a short beckoning motion that means go on. His lips stay closed.\n[Shot 2] At 00:02.000, closer on 小唐 (S4) standing on the open floor beside the desk: she draws her shoulders up, keeps her eyes on the floor tiles and lets them flick once toward 苏小满 (S1), then away; she speaks in a small thin nervous Mandarin, fast and slightly breathy: [Chinese] 钱经理。中午，我看见她往兜里塞东西。没看清。\n[Shot 3] At 00:08.400, reverse onto 苏小满 (S1) across the desk: her shoulders stay level, only her eyes travel to the girl by the door.\n[Shot 4] At 00:09.400, close on 钱经理 (S3) taking that in, the corner of his mouth pulling up, his lips closed for the rest of the shot.",
    "lean_anchor": "The whole clip takes place in one small private office and the camera never leaves it. The room has four plain white walls, a grey metal filing cabinet along the far wall, a long wooden desk standing across the middle of the floor, and venetian blinds on the right-hand wall laying bright bands of light across the desk top and the floor. A closed wooden door is set flat into the back wall, its surface plain wood with a small silver handle. Everything in this room reads as an office interior: the desk, the cabinet, the blinds and the plain painted walls. The walls behind the people are smooth painted plaster of one single light colour, unbroken and continuous from the skirting board up to the ceiling. All cardboard archive boxes and folders are plain brown corrugated cardboard. The people named in this beat are the only people in it: the manager stays behind the desk on the far side, the cleaner stays at the near end of it with her back to the camera, and the colleague stands where this beat places her. The count does not change.",
    "lean_shots": "[Shot 1] Medium: 钱经理 (S3) finishes looking at the colleague and turns his eyes to her face, waiting; he lifts one hand off the desk and turns it over, palm up, a short beckoning motion that means go on. His lips stay closed.\n[Shot 2] At 00:02.000, closer on 小唐 (S4) standing on the open floor beside the desk: she draws her shoulders up, keeps her eyes on the floor tiles and lets them flick once toward 苏小满 (S1), then away; she speaks in a small thin nervous Mandarin, fast and slightly breathy: [Chinese] 钱经理。中午，我看见她往兜里塞东西。没看清。\n[Shot 3] At 00:08.400, reverse onto 苏小满 (S1) across the desk: her shoulders stay level, only her eyes travel to the girl by the door.\n[Shot 4] At 00:09.400, close on 钱经理 (S3) taking that in, the corner of his mouth pulling up, his lips closed for the rest of the shot."
